task_master Debian packaging

The internal Debian package ID is task-master because Debian package IDs
cannot contain underscores. The application and executable are task_master.

The package installs the unprivileged desktop in /usr/bin/task_master and its
headless hardware collector in /usr/libexec/task_master/collector. postinst grants
only CAP_PERFMON to that collector. The collector opens package-energy counters
and drops the capability before sampling. The grant requires Linux 5.8+ and a
filesystem supporting Linux file capabilities. A failed grant fails package
configuration with a diagnostic rather than silently removing CPU power.

GLFW 3.4 is shipped privately in /usr/lib/task_master, preserving both Wayland and
X11 behavior on distributions whose system GLFW is older. FreeType and the
libraries linked by GLFW are resolved through generated Debian dependencies.
X11, Wayland and libdecor runtime packages are declared explicitly because GLFW
loads them dynamically; their absence must not remove either display backend.
Vulkan uses the host's Vulkan loader and graphics drivers. OpenSSH uses the
user's existing keys, agent and configuration.

Installing, upgrading or removing the package never enables background
persistence for users, deletes their saved settings/history, or changes their
user services. Persistence remains an in-app choice.

Build on a matching Debian/Ubuntu architecture after building the native app
and collector. dpkg-shlibdeps uses the build host's actual symbol metadata to
calculate minimum library versions; build release binaries on the oldest
supported distribution rather than transferring binaries from a newer host.
